invalid.jsx:2:12 lint/nursery/useConsistentTailwindVariableSyntax  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i Use modern CSS variable syntax in Tailwind classes.
  
    1 │ // Invalid: using var() syntax when simpler syntax available
  > 2 │ <div class="bg-[var(--my-color)]" />;
      │            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ <div class="text-[var(--brand-primary)]" />;
    4 │ <div class="border-[var(--border-color)]" />;
  
  i Replace: `bg-[var(--my-color)]` → `bg-[--my-color]`
  
  i The modern syntax `[--var-name]` is shorter and cleaner than `[var(--var-name)]`.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Safe fix: Use modern CSS variable syntax.
  
    2 │ <div·class="bg-[var(--my-color)]"·/>;
      │                 ----          -      

